# Merge drivers for files many agents edit at once. They act only in a clone
# that ran scripts/install-merge-drivers (the fast lane's scratch clone does;
# scripts/cloud-setup.sh does); elsewhere git merges by lines as before.
# GitHub's own merge ignores this file, so it helps local merges and rebases
# and the lane's integration of a conflicting PR, not the squash itself.
#
# json: three-way merge by object key (scripts/merge-json). C4 parts, .wave.json
# feature data, mutation plans and the audit baseline are objects whose keys
# different PRs add or change; two PRs touching different keys no longer
# conflict. Arrays stay atomic.
*.json merge=json

# No `merge=union`: it appends both sides' new lines in arbitrary order, so it
# fits only a shared file that is append-only and order-free. The audit of
# dev (2026-10-16) found none: docs/leads/*/timeline.tsv has one writer on its
# own lead/<feature> branch, every numbered table or list is ordered, and
# there is no changelog. Add one here only for a file that fits.
